# Link proves that `cells` of a line holds whole numbers, not that each fits an int32. Such a list is asked in front of a loop for storage of doubles that admits int32s; a for-of over it whose value is a key was not built twice at all:
# the read under the key stayed the form for any key. Where the loop takes the elements for keys the list is asked for storage of int32s: a key past 2^31 names no place, so a list of keys holds int32s.
# The value that the step hands out is then an int32 or a hole, and the list under it is tested in front as well. `sum` takes the same elements for numbers: there nothing is asked for storage of int32s alone.
# f1 = sum, f3 = count
# RUN(KEYS): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# KEYS: = HasArrayStorage {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32
# KEYS: isLoopHead=true
# KEYS: = IsElementPresent {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32
# KEYS: i32 @Int32 = GetArrayElement {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32 level=Proven [keyIsIntegral, isInBounds, isPresent]
# KEYS: = GetArrayElement {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32 level=Proven [keyIsIntegral]
# RUN(NUMBERS): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# NUMBERS-NOT: = HasArrayStorage {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32
